# Code Conventions

## Components

- Functional components + hooks ONLY (no class components)
- Props interface: `{ComponentName}Props`
- Named exports only (no default exports)
- Colocated tests: `ComponentName.test.tsx`

## TypeScript

- Strict mode — no `any`, no `@ts-ignore`
- Prefer `type` over `interface` for simple types
- Import types: `import type { X } from "..."`

## Files

- kebab-case for files: `element-utils.ts`
- PascalCase for components: `LayerUI.tsx`

## How to verify

- Run `yarn test:typecheck` and `yarn test:code` on the branch.
- In changed TS/TSX: no new `export default` on components; no new `class ... extends` React components.
- Search the diff for `@ts-ignore` and unjustified `any` — should be absent in new/edited code.
- New components: file is PascalCase `*.tsx`; colocated `ComponentName.test.tsx` exists when behavior is non-trivial.